findings.description:
`build_feedback_records()` documents `immune_result` as containing `cell_verdicts`, `final_verdicts`, and `rejected_findings`, but the implementation never reads `immune_result.rejected_findings`.

Location:

`bench/logs/exp40_slice_records_20260518T160503Z/working/_feedback_records_slice.py`, inside `build_feedback_records()`:
final_verdicts = getattr(immune_result, "final_verdicts", {}) or {}
cell_verdicts = getattr(immune_result, "cell_verdicts", {}) or {}
The function then iterates only:
for fid, verdict_list in cell_verdicts.items():
and later uses `final_verdicts.get(...)`, but there is no `getattr(immune_result, "rejected_findings", ...)` anywhere in the function.

Concrete counterexample:

model_responses.Gemini:
Addressing schema feedback from Round 2:
I formally withdraw the following findings as they are near-duplicates of existing canonical entries. I agree with the schema's assessment and will not pursue them further:
- Gemini_F004 is withdrawn (duplicate of Gemini_F002).
- Gemini_F006 is withdrawn (duplicate of Codex_C0009_EXT_FIX).
- Gemini_F003 is withdrawn (duplicate of Gemini_F001).
- Gemini_F005 is withdrawn (duplicate of DeepSeek_F002).

I also CONFIRM the following findings from other models:
CONFIRM C0022
CONFIRM C0023

FINDING_ID: C0020
SEVERITY: 0.90
FLAW_CLASS: 1
ABSTRACTION_INDEX: 0.60
FIND: The `finding_by_id` dictionary comprehension silently drops duplicate findings with the same `finding_id`. This causes feedback to be misrouted or lost when multiple models submit the same finding ID.
FOLLOW: When `finding_by_id` overwrites previous entries, any feedback (refutations, admissibility failures, duplicates, R_k discrepancies) for the overwritten models is lost. The feedback is only associated with the last model that submitted the finding ID. This breaks the core feedback loop for any model whose finding ID collided.
ANALYSE: CONFIRMED. HARD constraint violation (data loss / incorrect feedback routing). The comprehension `{f.finding_id: f for f in findings}` inherently keeps only the last element for each key.
